    "content": {
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Using Fick's law, explain how the alveoli are adapted for efficient gas exchange.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(4)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Rate of diffusion is proportional to surface area × concentration difference ÷ thickness of the exchange surface</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Many alveoli provide a large surface area</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Walls one cell thick give a short diffusion distance</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Ventilation and blood flow maintain a steep concentration gradient</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
  },
